  "query_preview": "..\n(Monday night through next Saturday)\nIssued at 1219 PM CST Sun Nov 15 2026\n\nShort wave ridging will move overhead during the second half of the \nday on Monday. this ridging will move east on Tuesday as a short \nwave trough tracks out of the Great Basin into the Intermountain \nWest of Utah. A response at the surface will occur on Tuesday ahead \nof this short wave with surface cyclogenesis centered over Wyoming \nas well as a surface pressure trough extending southward through \neastern New Mexico. Although we will see an increase in the surface \nwind speeds on Tuesday afternoon, southerly to slightly \nsoutheasterly flow will persist. Low status may again hang on \nthrough the area on Wednesday. At the moment, some clearing from the \nwest may be possible late in the afternoon, therefore, the \ntemperature forecast is highly uncertain. Another upper level trough \nwill load up in the western CONUS beginning on Thursday. Strong low \nlevel moisture advection will occur in advance of this system as it \nmoves across the Intermountain West. Lift from this trough will be \ndisplaced well to the north of the area leading to low precipitation \nchances. Low stratus again looks like the most likely outcome from \nthis system which could produce very light rain or drizzle late this \nweek.",
